{
 "schema": "checkpath.parser-divergence/v1",
 "note": "FIX-P0-06 tab parity fixtures: PyYAML's scanner rejects a tab character anywhere except inside a single/double-quoted scalar, inside a block scalar's content, or inside a comment — before/after a colon, after an alias, after a plain scalar, after a comma / `{` / `-` / `?`, after an anchor/tag, and inside a plain scalar, in block and flow context alike. The TypeScript `yaml` package accepted tabs as separation in all those positions. The TypeScript side now rejects the same shapes through hasRejectedTab (src/core/workflow-parser.ts) with the identical yaml_parse_error, in both parseWorkflowYaml and extractJobs. Tabs inside quoted scalars, block scalar content, and comments are deliberately NOT rejected — both sides already agree on them. See README.md in this directory and ADR FIX-P0-06 in handoff/P020-FIX-P0-06/TASK_REPORT.md.",
